# Andalusian Cadence with Rasgueado (repertoire plan: st-andalusian-cadence). An original study on
# the Spanish descending progression Am G F E, one bar each, four times, ending on E: the home chord
# of E Phrygian (the notes of A minor, centred on E). Shapes: Am (x02210), G (320003), the small
# F (xx3211), E (022100).
# Your part, every bar: a four-finger rasgueado on beat 1, written as four even sixteenth-note
# downstrokes (little finger, ring, middle, index flicking out one after another), then a thumb
# downstroke on beats 2 and 3. The last bar holds the second thumb stroke.
# Bars 9-16: a short melody in E Phrygian over the same chords (teacher's part, or yours once the
# strumming is easy). Each bar's first note is in its chord: bars 9-12 sigh down by step, E F E,
# D E D, C D C, B C B A B; bars 13-16 run up from A, fall from G and climb an F chord to F, which
# falls a half step to E, the Phrygian close. Over the E chord the melody leaves out G and G#.
title: Andalusian Cadence with Rasgueado
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original study on the Andalusian cadence
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 5
tags: flamenco, rasgueado, andalusian cadence, phrygian, spanish
tempo: 80
time: 3/4
key: E Phrygian

